#---
# purpose: "a guard naming a name only a sibling clause binds is undefined"
# expect: diagnostic
#---
#
# # head_guard_pins_nothing
#
# A clause guard sees the names its own head binds. A sibling clause's
# parameters are not in scope, and a `def` head has nothing bound before it, so
# `when a > y` under a head that binds `y` reaches for a binding that does not
# exist. Elixir rejects the same clause.
#
# The second clause here is live: the first clause only matches a literal, so
# nothing prunes the guard away before it is read.
def main() do
  dbg(live(1, 0))
end

defp live(1, _), do: :one
defp live(_, y) when a > y, do: :other
